        arc:
          'His life is told entirely in retrospect, in fragments scattered across the novel: the island boy, the young actor, the three marriages, the career, the growing loneliness of a man photographed constantly and known by almost nobody. The novel is unsparing about his selfishness and equally clear that his casual generosities outlive him, since a comic book he handed to a child and a paperweight he passed along end up carrying meaning through the entire post-collapse world. He dies in the first chapter and remains the center of the book, connected to nearly every major character by a thread none of them can see. That is the novel’s thesis about influence, delivered through a man who never learns he had any.',
